Description: unisoc: don't bring a stack up on an empty SIM slot
 The power-up from +CFUN: 0 attached both slots unconditionally, so whenever
 one of them was empty it ran +SFUN=2 and +SFUN=4 for a slot holding no card,
 and the CP asserted: 'modem cmd Modem Assert: T_P_ATC PS CP assert in file
 mnphone_api.c line 7401' -- seen on the E5 on 2026-10-04 with a card in slot 1
 and slot 2 empty, every single time ModemManager started (the power-up is
 replayed from the cached events, so the assert is not a one-off).  An assert
 silences the CP's AT server until the CP is reset, and modem_control left on
 its own does that only after minutes, so every command afterwards times out;
 ModemManager marks the modem invalid after ten of them and drops it, mmcli
 then answers 'No modems were found', and the card that really is in the phone
 is unreadable.  The slots holding a card are now read first, with
 +SPACTCARD=n;+CCID? on each (an error or an empty +CCID: is no card, the same
 test the SIM list uses), and only those get their SIM power, work mode and
 stack.  With nothing in either slot the stacks stay off instead of being
 raised on air; +CFUN? is still asked, so a modem with no card at all is
 reported the way it was before.
Author: e5-linux
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/src/plugins/unisoc/mm-broadband-modem-unisoc.c
